From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: access key scopes, key tip placement, IsDisplayModeEnabledChanged

Access keys now follow their scopes: the keys inside an element marked IsAccessKeyScope show and work only after that element's own key has been typed (so a scope and the top may use the same letters), AccessKeyScopeOwner puts an element into another's scope, and Escape goes back out of a scope before it leaves display mode. An element whose ExitDisplayModeOnAccessKeyInvoked is False keeps display mode on. Key tips honour KeyTipPlacementMode (bottom, top, left, right, centre or hidden) and their horizontal and vertical offsets. AccessKeyManager.IsDisplayModeEnabledChanged is raised when display mode starts and ends. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
